 - **Searching:** Items come in Red (Military), Yellow (Technical), Green (Medical) — findable via the Search Action (an Action card) — plus Blue (Crafted, never found by searching). The Item drawn must match the searched Room's color (background color under its name); in a **white** Room, choose any of the 3 decks. Per the rulebook's example: a Search draws 2 cards from one deck, keeps 1, and puts the other face down at the **bottom** of that deck (FAQ Actions 6). Each Search lowers the Room's Item Counter by 1; at 0 the Room is emptied and cannot be searched (exception: the Scout's Scavenging Action). **The Nest and Room Covered With Slime explicitly prohibit any Search Action** (original manual page 25).
 - **Crafting:** you may look through the Craft deck at any time; its cards are only ever taken via the Craft Item Basic Action (discard 2 Items whose blue Component icons match the Crafted card's 2 gray icons). The four Crafted Items and their component symbols (manual page 23) are: **Antidote = flame + medical cross; Taser = battery/lightning + screwdriver/tool; Flamethrower = flame + screwdriver/tool; Molotov Cocktail = flame + folded cloth/fabric.** These are component symbols: discard two Items showing the matching blue icons, rather than assuming a particular Item name.
 
+### Item and Weapon effects illustrated in the manual
+
+These examples come from the original manual's card illustrations (pp.22–23). In the following table, each Item costs **1 Action card**, is **One Use Only**, and is discarded after use. Choose only one effect when a card gives alternatives.
+
+| Item | Combat restriction | Effect |
+|---|---|---|
+| Bandages | Out of Combat only | **Dress 1 Serious Wound OR Heal all Light Wounds.** Dressing does not Heal or discard a Serious Wound. |
+| Clothes | Out of Combat only | **Discard your Slime marker OR Dress 1 Serious Wound.** |
+| Fire Extinguisher | May be used in Combat | **Discard Fire from your current Room OR choose 1 Intruder in your current Room and force it to Retreat.** It does not combine both effects or affect all Intruders like Fire Control System. |
+| Taser | May be used in Combat | Choose **1 Intruder in your Room**: it suffers **1 Injury and Retreats**. OR choose **1 Character in your Room**: they discard **all cards in their hand**, including Contamination cards. |
+| Energy Charge | Out of Combat only | **Fully load 1 of your own Energy Weapons** (up to its Ammo capacity) OR **Open or Close 1 Door in a Corridor connected to your Room**. The normal prohibition on closing Destroyed Doors applies. To reload someone else's Weapon, Trade the Charge to them first; you cannot use it directly on their Weapon. |
+| Molotov Cocktail | May be used in Combat | Choose your Room or a neighboring Room **containing an Intruder** (uncarried Eggs also permit the target, as under Eggs). **Place Fire** there; immediately, **each Intruder suffers 1 Injury and each Character suffers 1 Serious Wound**, including you if you are there. This immediate damage is separate from later Fire damage. |
+
+The illustrated **Six Shooter** is a Classic Weapon with Ammo capacity 6: it can only be reloaded with a **Reload Action card**, and a **single-crosshair** result deals **1 additional Injury** (2 total before other modifiers). The illustrated **Flamethrower** is a Classic Weapon with Ammo capacity 4: when shooting it always deals at least **1 Injury except on the blank miss face**, even if the rolled Intruder symbol would normally miss that target. A **two-crosshair** result deals the normal 2 Injuries and also places a Fire marker in **your Room**. Apply normal Shoot costs, targeting and Injury Effect checks; marker limits still apply. Flamethrower reloading uses Chemicals as described in the FAQ below.
+
+### Illustrated Quest Items
+
+Each activation below is a **cost-1 Basic Action, out of Combat**. It flips the Quest card into its active Item; a Room Malfunction does not prevent this activation. Using the active Item is a separate Action, also **cost 1 and out of Combat** for these examples.
+
+| Quest Item | Activation location | Active Item effect |
+|---|---|---|
+| Pilot's Evacuation Key | Fire Control System Room | In an **Evacuation Section Room**, Lock or Unlock **1 Pod in that Section**, subject to the occupied-Pod restriction. **One Use Only**: discard after use. It is neither remote nor reusable. |
+| Captain's Log Key | Comms Room | In a Room with an **available Computer**, look at the retained Objective cards of a chosen player; their Character need not share your Room. **One Use Only**: discard after use. A Malfunction makes the Computer unavailable even though it did not prevent activation. |
+| Mechanic's Plasma Torch | Storage Room | Open or Close **1 Door in a Corridor connected to your Room**; this Item can Close a **Destroyed** Door. It is reusable (not marked One Use Only). |
+
 ### Attacking other players
 
 Characters can never directly attack other Characters (anti-aggression implants) — but they may harm them indirectly: locking someone in a burning Room, activating Self-Destruct with people aboard, throwing a Grenade into a Room with other crew, etc.
